  "findings": [
    "One-SD ESD subcircuits allocated three slots while fixed legacy substrate index3 was read out of bounds. Both polarity crashes reproduced; allocation witness confirms sd1/slots4 in private repair.",
    "Allocation repair reserves the fixed four positions while SD iteration retains its original count; it does not invent a fourth electrical terminal.",
    "Allocation-only pilot exposes real missing VDD/gate-terminal connection for both polarities and remains rejected.",
    "Native cross-plane subcircuit gate callback uses exact native connectivity mask and positive-area overlap with an actual conducting tile. The point lies inside that intersection, with no node-name inference or body union.",
    "Both single polarity outputs preserve full three-terminal device contraction through1104/1091 actual positive native resistor edges and all collapsed capacitance, but this is not device attachment-point or RF validation.",
    "32-ESD,24-HBT and full351-device regressions all exit0 yet remain rejected for actual missing-terminal/extraction errors and/or incomplete output.",
    "32-ESD retains31 substrate misses; HBT24 retains24 gate and24 terminal misses plus1 failed net; full351 retains122 substrate,72 gate,98 terminal misses plus64 failed nets.",
    "No installed or previously frozen runtime, technology, original device geometry, netlist or thresholds changed.",
    "Only ResUtils.c and ResBasic.c change; no header or ABI changes. Their resis objects and module were rebuilt and the isolated runtime relinked.",
    "Split-tile cross-plane gate attachment is intentionally unsupported and will retain a terminal failure; no point approximated outside an actual rectangle."
  ],
